  "reasoning": "The claim originates from a widely cited March 2023 report by Goldman Sachs economists (Hatzius et al.). However, stating that generative AI \"will replace 300 million jobs worldwide\" misrepresents the report's actual findings. \n\nGoldman Sachs estimated that generative AI could *expose* the equivalent of roughly 300 million full-time jobs to automation globally. Crucially, the authors emphasized that exposure does not equate to outright job replacement. The report noted that for the vast majority of occupations, generative AI would partially automate tasks and complement workers rather than substitute them entirely. Additionally, the authors noted that technological displacement historically leads to new job creation and estimated a significant boost to global GDP over time. Presenting a scenario of task exposure as a definitive prediction of 300 million lost jobs is misleading.",
